            <ArticleTitle>&quot;No-vent&quot; technique of coronary artery bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>191-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isolated coronary artery bypass grafting was performed in 100 patients without the use of a left ventricular vent. Distention of the left ventricle did not occur. There was 1 late death unrelated to this technique. Vents in the left heart are not required under most circumstances.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
